      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core Function:** Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content (if it existed) or a note that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n**Rollback Capability:** If an agent run fails (due to a turn cap exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n\n**Transaction Semantics:** This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself acts as a transaction log, held in the process\u0027s memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Query Agent Note:** The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the journal\u0027s rollback path since it has no write tool at all\u2014the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
      "input_tokens": 5323,
      "output_tokens": 236
    }
